# Rukn Design System

Rukn is an AI-ready, RTL-first design system for Arabic, Urdu, and multilingual apps.

## Read first

1. [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)
2. [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md)
3. [`components.json`](../../components.json) — machine-readable catalog
4. [`docs/COMPONENT_API.md`](../../docs/COMPONENT_API.md)

## Bootstrap

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/design-system-variables.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/design-system.css">
<script src="components/rukn-navbar.js" defer></script>
<script src="components/rukn-ui.js" type="module"></script>
```

CDN:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/mfaizanatiq/RuknDesignSystem@master/dist/rukn.min.css">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/mfaizanatiq/RuknDesignSystem@master/dist/rukn.min.js" defer></script>
```

## Always

- Compose with Rukn primitives only: `btn-*`, `ds-*`, `rukn-*`
- Default theme is dark: `<html class="dark">`
- For Arabic: `lang="ar" dir="rtl"`; for Urdu: `lang="ur" dir="rtl"`
- Use tokens: `hsl(var(--primary))`, `var(--r-space-4)`, `var(--r-radius-lg)`
- Prefer `<rukn-navbar>`, `<rukn-footer>`, `<rukn-sidebar>` for chrome
- Prefer CSS classes (`btn-primary`, `ds-card`) for simple surfaces; Web Components for interactive chrome

## Never

- Do not invent class names outside the Rukn vocabulary
- Do not add Tailwind, Bootstrap, or MUI unless the user asks
- Do not hardcode hex colors when a token exists
- Do not skip RTL setup for Arabic/Urdu content
- Do not rebuild navbars when `<rukn-navbar>` covers the need

## Component shortcuts

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Primary action | `btn-primary` or `<rukn-button variant="primary">` |
| Card | `ds-card` or `<rukn-card>` |
| Input | `ds-input` or `<rukn-input>` |
| Badge | `ds-badge ds-badge-success` |
| App nav | `<rukn-navbar current="home">` |
| Live gallery | `components.html` |

## Prompt pattern

```
Use Rukn (AGENTS.md + DESIGN.md + components.json).
Build: [screen]. Locale: [en|ar|ur]. Theme: dark.
Primitives only. Include rukn-navbar for app pages.
```
